# Turn records for GLM-5.3-Flash on the parallel engine (--parallel above 1), kept inside the spill tier (0110). A
# record is the exact tokens the engine read and wrote for a conversation's turn, thinking included, so that a later
# request from a client that drops the thinking can be mapped back onto them (9005). It is two plain fields of the
# kept prompt state the reply ends on (decode.Snapshot): turn_key, the label and checks a lookup needs, and turn, the
# body. The tier writes a state when it is kept, before its reply's record exists, so the record follows the state:
# BlockStore.attach_record puts the body in the point's own file (<key>.rec) and the label in the point's json fields,
# which the tier's scan keeps in RAM; a record that lands while its state still waits to be written goes out with it,
# its file before the json. A record goes when its point goes and counts toward the cap; a restart keeps a label only
# with its file at its size, a read checks the file's CRC-32, and a state read back takes its record (read beside its
# small state, on the reader thread, never on the engine loop). Both ranks write every state when it is kept, as
# without records; rank 0 alone attaches one. A turn's label names it by what a client sends back of it: one sha256
# pass over the request's render, fed each span as length-prefixed raw bytes, reasoning left out, under a namespace of
# the tokenizer, chat template, clear_thinking, checkpoint and TF_GLM_LABEL_SALT (optional). At the end of an eligible
# reply, on the request thread and before the closing event, the reply alone continues the request's label pass, and
# the record lands on the request's own kept state unless it would replace another branch's record; a new state takes
# the record of the state it resumed from when its prompt continues that record's tokens. No record for a reply the
# model did not end, thinking off, pictures, draft:false, ignore_eos, chat_template_kwargs beyond the allowed ones,
# several engine runs, a tool call before </think>, a call the server closed or cut, reasoning over 65,536 tokens or a
# reasoning loop: each a cache miss later, never an error. Rank 0 only; nothing here can fail a reply or raise into the
# engine; alone it changes nothing a request is served. mgllm, 2026-10-07 (on the spill tier's blocks: 2026-10-13).
# Tests: tests/test_9004_labels.py, tests/test_9004_records.py, tests/test_9004_kept_records.py,
# tests/test_9004_spill_records.py (CPU; the first two need TF_GLM_TEST_MODEL_DIR).

